```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
            margin: 0;
        }
        .joke-container {
            text-align: center;
            background: #fff;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
        }
        h1 {
            color: #333;
        }
        .joke {
            color: #555;
            margin: 10px 0;
            font-size: 1.2em;
        }
        .punchline {
            color: #999;
            display: none;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="joke-container">
        <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
        <div class="joke">
            [Funny Joke]
        </div>
        <div class="punchline">
            [push to reveal punchline]
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        document.querySelector('.joke').addEventListener('click', function() {
            document.querySelector('.punchline').style.display = 'block';
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a basic webpage with a joke and a punchline hidden by default. When the joke area is clicked, the punchline is revealed. Customize the joke and styling as needed!
